From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:55:45 +0900
Subject: Virtual backend: render on a named GPU node that is not a DRM device

RUNGIC_KWIN_RENDER_DEVICE names the GPU node the virtual backend renders on (e.g. KGSL's
/dev/kgsl-3d0 in an Android container): libdrm does not list such a node, so the backend found no
device and fell back to QPainter (no screencast, no ScreenShot2, no dmabuf). The EGL display is
told the node (EGL cannot tell on a non-DRM device) and clients get zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 v3 at
most, as with the Android backend: v4 and later name the render node as main device, which
clients' Mesa cannot use. Unset, nothing changes.

Agent workspaces use it to run with no Android host, so they keep working while the phone is
asleep and the Rungic app frozen (docs/research/97, approach C).

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-02
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [generic: virtual backend on non-DRM GPU nodes]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:workspace.headless (to write)
